      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Let's solve the given problem step by step.\n\n1. **Solve the equation involving \\( x \\):**\n\n   The first given equation is:\n   \\[\n   2x + 7 = 3\n   \\]\n\n   To isolate \\( x \\), we first subtract 7 from both sides of the equation:\n   \\[\n   2x + 7 - 7 = 3 - 7\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this, we get:\n   \\[\n   2x = -4\n   \\]\n\n   Next, we divide both sides by 2:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2x}{2} = \\frac{-4}{2}\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this, we find:\n   \\[\n   x = -2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the second equation:**\n\n   Now we use the value of \\( x \\) in the second equation:\n   \\[\n   bx - 10 = -2\n   \\]\n\n3. **Solve for \\( b \\):**\n\n   Replace \\( x \\) with \\(-2\\) in the equation:\n   \\[\n   b(-2) - 10 = -2\n   \\]\n\n   Simplify the equation:\n   \\[\n   -2b - 10 = -2\n   \\]\n\n   Add 10 to both sides to isolate the term with \\( b \\):\n   \\[\n   -2b - 10 + 10 = -2 + 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   -2b = 8\n   \\]\n\n   Finally, divide both sides by \\(-2\\) to solve for \\( b \\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{-2b}{-2} = \\frac{8}{-2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   b = -4\n   \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\n\n\\(\\boxed{-4}\\)",
